#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ Lsp (LSP semantics over JsonRpcCl, ADR D16) against a real language
⍝ server, pyright-langserver — installed ad hoc via `npx -y -p pyright
⍝ pyright-langserver --stdio` (see the Tutorial's Step 5/6 and ADR
⍝ D13/D16 for why `-p pyright` matters). Needs network access and an
⍝ npm install on first run, same caveat as JsonRpcCl's own manual
⍝ real-server verification — not run in a hypothetical CI without
⍝ network access.
⎕IO←1
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/JsonRpcCl.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Lsp.dyalog'

opts←(Timeout:90)
h←opts Lsp.Connect'cmd.exe' '/C' 'npx' '-y' '-p' 'pyright' 'pyright-langserver' '--stdio'
⎕←'connected, capabilities: ',⍕h.ServerCapabilities.⎕NL ¯2

fixture←'D:\devel\mcp-client\examples\hover-fixture.py'
tie←fixture ⎕NTIE 0
text←⎕NREAD tie 82(⎕NSIZE tie)
⎕NUNTIE tie
slashed←fixture ⋄ slashed[⍸slashed='\']←'/'
uri←'file:///',slashed

h Lsp.DidOpen(uri text 'python')
⎕←'didopen sent'

⍝ 'os.getcwd()' is on line 3 (1-based in the file, 0-based on the
⍝ wire — LSP positions are always 0-based, unrelated to ⎕IO); hover
⍝ over 'getcwd' (character 3, 0-based, inside the word).
r←h Lsp.Hover(uri 2 4)
⎕←'hover result: ',r.contents.value

⍝ A position with genuinely nothing to say (a blank line) legitimately
⍝ comes back as JSON null — ordinary data, not a signal (see
⍝ Lsp.Hover's own comment and ADR D16).
r2←h Lsp.Hover(uri 1 0)
⎕←'no-hover-info result is JSON null: ',⍕r2≡⊂'null'

Lsp.Disconnect h
⎕←'status after disconnect=',h.JsonRpcCl.Status
⎕OFF
